==Strategy==
This is a simple [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] stage with Dread Bore as a secondary pusher and random [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] peons to mix things up. As you might be realizing, like the first two [[Zero Legends]] stages Puffzerker's been in the best way to kill them is to just get a good chain on them with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. From there, it should be really easy to get high damage onto Puffzerker by simply luring them and then beating them to death with Bahamut, and then chipping any bit of health that remains with good [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]]. From there, your next goal is fighting off the Dread Bore and Professor A. at the same time. Unfortunately for Professor A., [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cat]] has way too much health against Red enemies. Force the Dread Bore to the surface with a Holy Blast, then use either [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] or a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] alongside Rappers and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] as well as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to chip him down. While the Jackrabbits and other peons might be annoying, Newtone's huge damage ensures they'll take damage knockbacks, and if he isn't ready to attack yet you can always use Dread Bore as a stepping stone for Jelly Dumpling or Housewife hits. Even if Dread Bore doesn't get Z-Killed, you can simply repeat this process again to kill the Dread Bore for good and the Professor A. soon after.

